Thank you very much for your thoughtful engagement throughout the discussion and for the constructive follow-ups. We’re glad the additional analyses were useful, and we appreciate your concluding assessment.

As for a summary, in our final revision, we will:

- report balanced MAE alongside MAE in all relevant tables and clearly describe the macro-averaging procedure;
- include histograms of target distributions (raw and quantized) for representative metrics and briefly explain the percentile-based binning;
- clarify the selection of beam size B and point readers to the ablation that studies its effect;
- add the new teacher-forced (ground-truth-injected) decoding ablation in the appendix to quantify error propagation, across dev/test subsets it reduces MAE by ~25–50% relative to fully reference-free decoding; we will include the table and discuss the resulting efficiency–accuracy trade-off;
- keep our discussion of ordinal-aware objectives as a forward direction and soften any language that might imply it is already solved within our framework;
- expand the limitations/societal impact section to emphasize responsible use and the continued importance of human evaluation.

Thank you again for the time and care you invested.

